**Wedge:** a "FOAK Tech-Risk Score" and lineage report for project lenders, infra funds and offtakers. It is built from the full graph of public R&D on a technology class:
- every DOE/ARPA-E/SBIR/Horizon/UKRI award;
- the goals each award claimed and whether the FTR says they were met;
- slips, follow-on funding and later commercial outcomes, including EIA-923 capacity factors for power plants.

Sell it as diligence software at $50-250k a year to roughly 200 climate infra funds, banks and corporate offtakers. Then become the data and pricing engine for an existing capacity provider (New Energy Risk, Ariel Green or a Lloyd's syndicate) on a share-of-premium basis, and only later run an MGA.

**Stronger reframe:** the defensible output is not "does tech X hit nameplate", which the data cannot label. It is a reference-class forecaster for scale-up slip and cost overrun, by technology class and scale step. The public record can label that: award timelines, no-cost extensions, follow-on phases and LPO conditional commitments that never close.
